          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Immanuel Kant</strong><br>\nImmanuel Kant was born on April 22, 1724, in Königsberg, Prussia. He was the fourth of nine children, but only five of them reached adulthood. Kant's parents were humble craftsmen, his father a harness maker. The family's financial status did not allow for lavish living, but they were devoted to their children's education. Education played a crucial role in his upbringing, with his pietistic family emphasizing schooling and hard work.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Education and Teaching</strong><br>\nKant was an exceptional student who attended the Collegium Fredericianum and later the University of Königsberg. He studied a broad range of subjects, including physics, mathematics, and philosophy. After university, he worked as a private tutor for several families, which gave him the financial stability to continue his own research and eventually return to the university to teach.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Early Works</strong><br>\nBefore his most famous works, Kant published scientific papers, including \"General Natural History and Theory of the Heavens\" in 1755. This work theorized the formation and rotation of planets and was important in the development of the nebular hypothesis. His early works laid the foundation for his later philosophical inquiries, as they demonstrated his acute interest in natural sciences and metaphysics.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
